/-!
# VII17 — finite-regularity analysis tools (B3 coordinate certificate, analysis layer)

Generic one-variable tools for the finite `C⁶` bootstrap at the compactified endpoint `x = 0⁺`:
* `PS g` — `g` is `C^∞` on a right neighbourhood of `0`; `RL k g` — `g, …, g⁽ᵏ⁾` have finite right limits;
  `ExtV k g L` — an independent `Cᵏ` extension across `0` agreeing with `g` on the positive side, value `L`.
* `extV_of_RL` — right limits ⇒ extension (accepted VII16 `glue`); `ExtV.RL` — the converse.
* `euler_lim` (L'Hôpital), `euler_RL` — `x M′ + (n+1) M = φ`, `x M → 0` transfers right limits from `φ` to `M`.
* `hadamard` — `G ∈ Cᵏ⁺¹`, `G(0)=0` ⇒ `G/x ∈ Cᵏ` (loses one order).
* `euler_gain` — `x g′ + 2 g = x H`, `g → 0`, `H ∈ Cᵏ` ⇒ `g ∈ Cᵏ⁺¹` (gains one order: `g′ = H − 2g/x`).
The endpoint condition `g → 0` excludes the homogeneous `c/x²` mode. No physics input.
-/

